DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_C23C_5112';
<p>c23c_5112</p> <p>In a standard dihybrid cross involving two independent genes, the expected F<sub>2</sub> phenotypic ratio is <b>9:3:3:1</b>. A test-cross with an F<sub>1</sub> individual and a double recessive usually yields a <b>1:1:1:1</b> phenotypic ratio if the genes assort independently.</p> <p>The progeny from the test-cross exhibited a modified ratio of <b>1:3</b>, different from the expected 1:1:1:1 ratio.</p> <p>What phenotypic ratio would be expected in the F<sub>2</sub> generation if the original dihybrid cross is continued?</p>
PROMPT_C23C_5112
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_1';
a ratio of 13:3
LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_2';
a ratio of 14:2
LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_3';
a ratio of 16:0
LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_4';
a ratio of 5:11
LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_5';
a ratio of 8:8
LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_5
$choice_6 = <<'LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_6';
a ratio of 9:7
LITERAL_C23C_5112_CHOICE_6
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_C23C_5112_CORRECT_1';
a ratio of 9:7
LITERAL_C23C_5112_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5, $choice_6);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->buttons\}
END_TEXT
ANS($answer->cmp);

ENDDOCUMENT();
